# Shell scripts must keep LF endings on every platform. Git's autocrlf default
# on Windows rewrites them to CRLF at checkout, which leaves a carriage return
# on the shebang: bash then looks for an interpreter named "bash\r" and the
# hook and MCP server fail with "No such file or directory". The repository
# blobs are already LF; this stops the checkout from changing them.
*.sh -text
